<ArticleLayout slug="one-app-vs-tool-stack-social-content" ctaLabel="Create your account" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">Judge them by the hand-offs. On one simple trace, a post made across five tools changes hands 17 times, and the approval covers a file and a text rather than the post that goes out. One app takes those moves out. A stack still wins where one expert does one deep job all day.</p>

  <h2>Is an all-in-one social media content tool better than a stack of tools?</h2>

  <p>For most teams making their own social posts, yes. The picture, the copy, the approval and the schedule live on one post, so nothing is exported or uploaded twice, and in an app like hubStudio the approved version is the one that publishes. A stack is better when one specialist job needs a deeper tool.</p>

