  <h2>Where does a social post change hands in each way of working?</h2>

  <p>Feature lists hide the real cost of a stack, which sits in the seams between tools. So follow one post.</p>

  <p>The trace below is deliberately simple: one LinkedIn post with one picture, one round of changes, then the same post adapted for Instagram. The stack has five tools (an image generator, an image editor, a shared file store, an approval tool and a scheduler), and the copy is written in an ordinary document. Each export, upload, rename and paste of the copy into another tool counts as one move.</p>

